<title>UK: UK June natural gas output falls 14 pct - Wood Mac.</title>
<headline>UK June natural gas output falls 14 pct - Wood Mac.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's natural gas  production continued its seasonal slide in June, falling 972 million cubic feet a day (mmcfd), or nearly 14 percent from May to some 6,172 mmcfd, industry consultants Wood Mackenzie said on Monday.</p>
<p>But production was around 20 percent up on June 1996.</p>
<p>The crop in supply was mirrored in demand on the Transco system which was down 586 mmcfd on May at 5,585 mmcfd.</p>
<p>Output from the giant Rough storage facility was more than matched by injections of gas, and production at the Centrica operated Morecambe Bay fields slipped by 15 percent to 284 mmcfd in June.</p>
<p>&quot;This seasonal decline in Morecambe's output has been demonstrated over the previous three years and is partly due to the operator's drive to optimise the tax position of the fields,&quot; Wood Mackenzie said.</p>
<p>Other significant declines were seen at the Beryl, Galleon, Jupiter, Bruce and Miller fields.</p>
<p>Production from Enterprise's Nelson field was down for the whole month as a result of a two week maintenance programme coupled with corrosion problems found in a gas compressor.</p>
